          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.108,
            0.887,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "6. A child has 2 shirts (one red and one blue) and 3 types of pants (jeans, khakis, and shorts). List all the possible combinations of outfits consisting of one shirt and one pair of pants. Display your answer in a table format."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.189,
            0.883,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "7. A tyre company records distances before replacement in 1000 cases."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.216,
            0.822,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "| Distance | Less than | 4001 to | 9001 to | More than |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| (km) | 4000 | 9000 | 14000 | 14000 |\n| Number of cases | 20 | 210 | 325 | 445 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_table_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.333,
            0.761,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "Find the probability that a randomly chosen tyre lasts:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.361,
            0.441,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": "(i) Less than 4000 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.383,
            0.548,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Between 4000 and 14000 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.405,
            0.464,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "(iii) More than 14000 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.435,
            0.884,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "8. The letters of the word ‘PEACE’ are placed on cards. Leela draws a card without looking."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.481,
            0.556,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": "(i) What is the probability that it is a P, E or C?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.597,
            0.48,
            0.817,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.529,
            0.683,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "(ii) What is the probability that it is not an E?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.559,
            0.883,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "\\*9. A game of chance consists of spinning an arrow (see Fig. 7.7.) which"
